{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.DiprotonSecondOrder"],"declarations":27,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.binding_of_closedForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.binding_of_closedForm","kind":"theorem","line":336,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonResponseClosedForm.lean#L336-L342","doc":"**What the carrier buys**: given the closed form, the binding computed from the measured\ntraces *is* the derived `Θ(h⁴)` quantity, so the ceiling above applies to it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.nucleonTrace_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.nucleonTrace_pos","kind":"theorem","line":323,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonResponseClosedForm.lean#L323-L334","doc":"`0 < tr(W_free)` on `q > 1`, so the ratio is well posed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.ResponseClosedForm.ratio_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.ResponseClosedForm.ratio_eq","kind":"theorem","line":321,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonResponseClosedForm.lean#L321-L321","doc":"The bond moves the trace by exactly the derived response. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.ResponseClosedForm.free_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.ResponseClosedForm.free_eq","kind":"theorem","line":319,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonResponseClosedForm.lean#L319-L319","doc":"The free trace factorises as the square of the single-nucleon `H₃` trace: disjoint-union\nmultiplicativity of the Markov trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.ResponseClosedForm.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.ResponseClosedForm.mk","kind":"ctor","line":316,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonResponseClosedForm.lean#L316-L316","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.ResponseClosedForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.ResponseClosedForm","kind":"structure","line":313,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonResponseClosedForm.lean#L313-L321","doc":"**The closed-form carrier.** `trFree` and `trAtom` are the `H₆` convention-D Markov traces\nof the two-nucleon word without and with the bond. Both fields are verified by the probe\nagainst two independent code paths; neither is proved in Lean. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.nucleonTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.nucleonTrace","kind":"def","line":309,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonResponseClosedForm.lean#L309-L311","doc":"The single nucleon's `H₃` convention-D Markov trace on the canonical 11-letter element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.binding_ceiling_on_interval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.binding_ceiling_on_interval","kind":"theorem","line":282,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonResponseClosedForm.lean#L282-L305","doc":"**A fully derived keV ceiling.** On `1 < q ≤ 23/20` the magnitude is at most `α/100`:\n`h⁴ ≤ 1/100` from the interval and `c ≤ 1` from the polynomial gap. Nothing measured enters —\n`α` is a closed form in `q` and the CAL-1 electron mass. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.diproton_unbound_of_response_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.diproton_unbound_of_response_closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":273,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonResponseClosedForm.lean#L273-L280","doc":"**For EVERY `q > 1` the γγ-selected diproton is unbound.** Derived: `c > 0` on the whole\nray forces `μ > 1`, and step 8's log law turns that into `B < 0`. No measurement enters. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.binding_magnitude_fourth_order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.binding_magnitude_fourth_order","kind":"theorem","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonResponseClosedForm.lean#L259-L271","doc":"**The headline.** Step 9's bracket instantiated at the derived `r`: both ends carry `h⁴`,\nso the γγ-selected diproton binding is `Θ(h⁴)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.ratio_deviation_is_fourth_order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.ratio_deviation_is_fourth_order","kind":"theorem","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonResponseClosedForm.lean#L252-L255","doc":"**`μ − 1 = h⁴·c`**: the interface ratio deviates at FOURTH order in the deformation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.respPP_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.respPP_pos","kind":"theorem","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonResponseClosedForm.lean#L243-L250","doc":"`0 < r(q)` for every `q > 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.respPP_eq_hSq_mul_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.respPP_eq_hSq_mul_coeff","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonResponseClosedForm.lean#L233-L241","doc":"**The factorisation — the step-9 correction in one line.** `r = h²·c`, because\n`(q² − 1)² = q²·h²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.responseCoeff_le_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.responseCoeff_le_one","kind":"theorem","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonResponseClosedForm.lean#L205-L231","doc":"**`c(q) ≤ 1` for every `q ≥ 1`** — again with no interval hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.coeff_gap_shifted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.coeff_gap_shifted","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonResponseClosedForm.lean#L192-L203","doc":"**The upper bound's mechanism**: `(q²+1)P − q²(q⁴+q²+1)R` re-expanded at `q = 1 + t` has\nevery coefficient non-negative, with constant term `5`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.responseCoeff_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.responseCoeff_pos","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonResponseClosedForm.lean#L182-L190","doc":"**`0 < c(q)` for every `q ≥ 1`** — with no interval hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.denom_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.denom_pos","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonResponseClosedForm.lean#L177-L180","doc":"The denominator is positive on `q ≥ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.respPP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.respPP","kind":"def","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonResponseClosedForm.lean#L173-L175","doc":"**`r(q)`**: the trace-weighted response `tr(W·D)/tr(W)` in closed form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.responseCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.responseCoeff","kind":"def","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonResponseClosedForm.lean#L169-L171","doc":"**`c(q)`**: the order-one coefficient of the response. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.responsePoly_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.responsePoly_pos","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonResponseClosedForm.lean#L163-L165","doc":"`0 < R(q)` for every `q ≥ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.one_le_responsePoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.one_le_responsePoly","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonResponseClosedForm.lean#L148-L161","doc":"`1 ≤ R(q)` for every `q ≥ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.nucleonPoly_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.nucleonPoly_pos","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonResponseClosedForm.lean#L144-L146","doc":"`0 < P(q)` for every `q ≥ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.four_le_nucleonPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.four_le_nucleonPoly","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonResponseClosedForm.lean#L121-L142","doc":"`4 ≤ P(q)` for every `q ≥ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.responsePoly_shifted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.responsePoly_shifted","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonResponseClosedForm.lean#L113-L119","doc":"**`R` re-expanded at `q = 1 + t`**, constant term `1`, all coefficients non-negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.nucleonPoly_shifted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.nucleonPoly_shifted","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonResponseClosedForm.lean#L101-L111","doc":"**`P` re-expanded at `q = 1 + t`: every coefficient is non-negative.** This is the whole\npositivity argument; the constant term is `4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.responsePoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.responsePoly","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonResponseClosedForm.lean#L97-L99","doc":"`R(q)`: the numerator of the `G³` response. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.nucleonPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DiprotonResponseClosedForm.nucleonPoly","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DiprotonResponseClosedForm.lean#L91-L95","doc":"`P(q)`: the numerator of the single nucleon's `H₃` convention-D Markov trace on the\ncanonical 11-letter element. ","signatureChunk":0}]}